{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Shall be put to death.</b> And the word <b>yeiḥeram</b> is from a binyan whose verbal noun is not named, like <b>ya'amod</b> <i>ḥai</i> [shall stand alive]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The example יעמד חי alludes to 2 Samuel 18:18; the point is that יחרם belongs to a binyan (nif'al) whose noun form lacks a standard name."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:01.899212713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}